  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5" extension="2015-08-01"/><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5.1" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Tiredness for some months and ankle swelling by evening, with a raised creatinine (1.42 mg/dL, race-free eGFR 40, confirmed at 38 with cystatin C) and albumin in the urine (240 mg/g) found today; cause and chronicity to be established</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R94.4</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting finding, superseded by the kidney diagnosis at two weeks.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Elevated blood pressure at intake (164/94 mmHg, average of two readings), without a diagnosis of hypertension; home readings for one week to confirm</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R03.0</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting finding, superseded by the confirmed diagnosis at two weeks.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Hypertension, stage 2, confirmed by home readings (average 150/88 mmHg), with chronic kidney disease</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>I12.9</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis; no blood pressure from her life is recorded.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Chronic kidney disease G3b A2 (eGFR 38 by creatinine and cystatin C, urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio 240 and 228 mg/g), present at least two years; small, echogenic kidneys without obstruction; most likely hypertensive kidney disease, with APOL1-associated disease possible; 5-year kidney failure risk about 7%</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>N18.32</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis linked to the kidney disease recorded at her death.</td>
  </tr>
